+# Request to sldb: resolve bare reference ids and report unresolved references
+
+Date: 2026-10-18. From: the deskops executor, for the coordinator of SLDB_1.
+Phase F4 of `runs/planning/deskops-rewrite-inventory.md`.
+
+## What deskops needs
+
+F4 replaces deskops' own regex edge extractor (`deskops/graph/extract_edges.py`) with
+sldb's edge index, so that one schema of node ids and one graph runtime are used. Two
+sldb behaviors block that today.
+
+1. `_ids_in` (`src/sldb/store/edge_index/declared_references.py:67-74`) keeps only
+   values written `Model:name`. deskops stores bare ids and paths:
+   `depends_on: [task-x]`, `inherits_from: [task-y]`, `from_drawer: desk/drawer/tasks/task-x.md`,
+   `pills: [desk/contexts/pill-x.md]`, `atoms: [desk/atoms/...]`. None of them emits an
+   edge, even when the target document is tracked.
+2. `resolve_edges` (`src/sldb/store/edge_index/resolve.py:23-34`) leaves out a schema edge
+   whose target is not a node, with no record of it (`kept` loses it; `problems` only
+   describes authored `relation_doc` edges). `deskops graph missing` therefore cannot use
+   the index to find dangling declared references.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+Environment: structuredLanguageDB 0.1.11, Python 3.13.5, deskops from this checkout.
+
+```bash
+export PYTHONPATH=/path/to/deskops-checkout
+rm -rf /tmp/sldb-repro-unresolved && mkdir /tmp/sldb-repro-unresolved
+cd /tmp/sldb-repro-unresolved && git init -q .
+
+deskops init .
+
+deskops add task --root . --title "Bare id repro" \
+  --goal "Show a bare id emits no edge" --scope "Throwaway repro" \
+  --implementation-path "none" --done-when "reproduced" \
+  --depends-on task-nope
+
+deskops add task --root . --title "Qualified id repro" \
+  --goal "Show a qualified id is declared and then dropped" --scope "Throwaway repro" \
+  --implementation-path "none" --done-when "reproduced" \
+  --depends-on TaskDoc:task-nope
+```
+
+The composed index has no `references` edge for either task:
+
+```console
+$ sldb edges show TaskDoc:task-bare-id-repro --relation references --store .sldb
+[]
+$ sldb edges show TaskDoc:task-qualified-id-repro --relation references --store .sldb
+[]
+```
+
+The unit below the index shows why. `declared_reference_edges` keeps the qualified value
+and drops the bare one before anything is resolved:
+
+```python
+from deskops.models import TaskDoc
+from sldb.store.edge_index.declared_references import declared_reference_edges
+
+payload = {"depends_on": ["task-nope", "TaskDoc:task-other"]}
+for edge in declared_reference_edges("TaskDoc", "task-source", TaskDoc, payload):
+    print(edge.model_dump())
+```
+
+```console
+{'source': 'sldb://document/TaskDoc:task-source', 'target': 'sldb://document/TaskDoc:task-other', 'relation': 'references', 'metadata': {'origin': 'schema', 'field': 'depends_on'}}
+```
+
+For the qualified value the edge is written into the document's shard:
+
+```console
+$ grep -A4 'relation: references' .sldb/runtime/edges/TaskDoc/task-qualified-id-repro.yaml
+  relation: references
+  metadata:
+    origin: schema
+    field: depends_on
+```
+
+but composing the index drops it because `TaskDoc:task-nope` is not a node, and reports
+nothing:
+
+```python
+from deskops.models import TaskDoc
+from sldb.store.edge_index.declared_references import declared_reference_edges
+from sldb.store.edge_index.resolve import resolve_edges
+
+edges = declared_reference_edges("TaskDoc", "task-source", TaskDoc, {"depends_on": ["TaskDoc:task-missing"]})
+kept, problems = resolve_edges({}, edges)
+print("declared:", [e.model_dump() for e in edges])
+print("kept:", kept)
+print("problems:", problems)
+```
+
+```console
+declared: [{'source': 'sldb://document/TaskDoc:task-source', 'target': 'sldb://document/TaskDoc:task-missing', 'relation': 'references', 'metadata': {'origin': 'schema', 'field': 'depends_on'}}]
+kept: []
+problems: []
+```
+
+## Proposed API
+
+### (a) Resolve a declared reference field's bare ids
+
+Add a per-field allowed-model declaration for reference fields, mirroring
+`__containment__` (which already maps a field to the models it may hold):
+
+```python
+class TaskDoc(OperationalArtifactDoc):
+    __containment__ = {
+        "current_node": ["RitualDoc"],
+        "pills": ["PillDoc"],
+        "atoms": ["AtomDoc"],
+    }
+    __references__ = ["references", "depends_on", "inherits_from", "from_drawer"]
+    __reference_models__ = {
+        "depends_on": ["TaskDoc"],
+        "inherits_from": ["TaskDoc"],
+        "from_drawer": ["TaskDoc"],
+        # `references` stays out: it is free-form (files, commits, commands).
+    }
+```
+
+Resolution rule for each value in a declared field, in this order:
+
+1. A value that already contains `:` is an export id and is used as written.
+2. A value that names a tracked document's project-relative path is resolved to that
+   document's node. `composition_targets._owners_by_path` already builds this map; a
+   declared reference should reuse it (normalize with `normpath`, strip backticks).
+3. A bare value whose field allows exactly one model is qualified as `Model:value`.
+4. A bare value with no allowed model, or with several, is left unresolved and reported
+   by (b). With several, report `ambiguous` rather than guessing.
+
+Containment should use the same rule: its allowed-model list already exists, but `_ids_in`
+ignores it, so `pills: [pill-x]` would resolve while `pills: [desk/contexts/pill-x.md]`
+needs rule 2.
+
+Notes for the design:
+
+- Keep `__references__` a list. A new dunder is backward compatible for existing models.
+  If it enters `_contract_parts` (`src/sldb/store/hashing.py:88-89`), every model contract
+  moves and each store needs `sldb stores update`; decide whether that migration is worth
+  it, or accept that changing the map does not trigger a rebuild.
+- Shards built under this rule differ, so `EDGE_INDEX_VERSION`
+  (`src/sldb/store/edge_index/node_ids.py:8`) must move from `3` to `4`.
+
+### (b) Report unresolved declared references
+
+```python
+sldb.api.unresolved_references(
+    store: str | Path | None,
+    include_linked: bool = True,
+    exclude_tags: Iterable[str] = (),
+) -> list[UnresolvedReference]
+```
+
+```python
+class UnresolvedReference(BaseModel):
+    source: str                  # export id, e.g. "TaskDoc:task-a"
+    model: str                   # "TaskDoc"
+    field: str                   # "depends_on"
+    target: str                  # value as written: "task-nope", "TaskDoc:task-x", a path
+    target_export_id: str | None # "TaskDoc:task-x" when only the target is missing
+    relation: str                # "references" or "contains"
+    reason: str                  # "missing_document" | "ambiguous" | "unknown_path"
+```
+
+- Fill it while composing, where `resolve_edges` already drops schema/alias edges. Keep
+  this list separate from `EdgeIndex.problems`: `problems` fails authored edges, while an
+  unresolved declared reference is a normal condition a caller inspects.
+- Expose it on `EdgeIndex` (e.g. `unresolved_references`) and as the public function
+  above. A CLI view such as `sldb edges unresolved [--store S]` would make it
+  inspectable; the API is what deskops calls.
+- Include only declared edges (`metadata.field` present), so alias edges are not reported
+  as references.
+
+## deskops caller
+
+`deskops.graph.checks.find_missing_graph_references(root, graph_path=None)` is the
+function to call it. It is reached from `deskops graph missing`
+(`deskops/cli/main.py:_graph_missing`) and from
+`deskops.operations.OperationService._build_atom_from_graph_finding`.
+
+Today it calls `deskops.graph.extract_edges.extract_declared_edges(root).missing_targets`
+and maps the result to `GraphMissingFinding(kind="missing_declared_target", ...)`. F4
+replaces that source with `sldb.api.unresolved_references(store)`, mapping `source` /
+`field` / `target` into the finding, and keeps the regex extractor only for file-path
+edges and provenance (`provenance_path`, `provenance_locator`) that sldb does not carry.
+The caller also needs the archived-record flag (`record: true`) that F0 added; it can
+read it from the source document's payload, or sldb can carry it in the record.
+
+## Response
+
+sldb-04, 2026-10-18 (through a cross-session message to the deskops supervisor): accepted (a) and (b) with changes; ships in structuredLanguageDB 0.1.12; sldb-04 sends the final shape for review before merging and announces the release.
+
+(a) `__reference_models__ = {"field": ["Model", ...]}` as proposed, with:
+1. Resolution at index composition, not in the shard: the shard keeps the value as written plus its field and allowed models, and `resolve_edges` resolves it against the nodes and tracked paths present at that moment (a shard is rebuilt only when its own document changes, so resolving there would go stale).
+2. Rules in order: a value with `:` is used as written; a value that is the path of a tracked document resolves to it (normpath, backticks stripped); a bare value is tried as `Model:value` for each allowed model: exactly one existing resolves, more than one is `ambiguous`, none is `missing_document`.
+3. A field with no declared models (deskops' free-form `references`) resolves only tracked paths and qualified ids; its bare values are not reported.
+4. `__containment__` applies the same rules with its allowed-model list, so `pills: [desk/contexts/pill-x.md]` resolves.
+5. Contract: `__reference_models__` enters the contract hash only when a model declares it; TaskDoc will show `contract moved` once deskops adds it (fix: `sldb stores update`). RelationDoc, RelationTypeDoc and RitualDoc are untouched.
+6. `EDGE_INDEX_VERSION` moves to 4; shards rebuild on their own.
+
+(b) `sldb.api.unresolved_references(store, include_linked=True, exclude_tags=()) -> list[UnresolvedReference]` with fields `source`, `model`, `field`, `target` (as written), `target_export_id` (None when it cannot be qualified), `relation` (`references` | `contains`), `reason` (`missing_document` | `ambiguous` | `unknown_path`) and `source_path`. Also exposed as `EdgeIndex.unresolved_references` (separate from `EdgeIndex.problems`) and as `sldb edges unresolved [--store S] [--format json]`. Only declared edges (with `metadata.field`) are included, not alias edges. `unknown_path` is a path-shaped value (contains `/` or ends in `.md`) that is not a tracked document, in a field with declared models or containment. No `record: true` flag: deskops reads it from the source document's payload through `source`.
+
+deskops accepted this shape on 2026-10-18. task-rw-f4-graph-on-sldb-edge-index requires structuredLanguageDB>=0.1.12.
